    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0757" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg663"/>

                <head>No. 415.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hubbard to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 2, 1887</date>.
                        (Received June 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 347.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inclose herewith a leading
                    editorial (as translated) from the Jiji Shimpo, in the bold and impartial spirit
                    which always characterizes that eminent Japanese journal. Its well-known
                    friendship for the United States is prominently expressed in this leader. I call
                    your attention expressly to the clipping herewith transmitted.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard B.
                    Hubbard</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d415-a1.xml" xpointer="d415-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
